# Test 3: (removed) parameter names via duckdb_functions()
# ========================================================
# The former assertions here checked `list_contains(parameters, '<argname>')` for
# the parse_ast / read_ast / ast_unparse_rules TABLE functions. That asserts
# DuckDB's catalog representation of table-function parameter names — a
# DuckDB-internal detail, not sitting_duck's documentation — and it differs by
# DuckDB version: on the v2.0 line `duckdb_functions().parameters` no longer
# surfaces positional table-function arg names (they show on v1.x), so
# `list_contains(parameters, 'code')` returns 0 there. It is NOT a sitting_duck
# doc gap (the functions still declare their args and carry descriptions/examples).
# Discoverability — the actual intent of this file — is verified by Tests 1, 2,
# and 4 against sitting_duck-controlled metadata (descriptions, examples, the
# sitting_duck category), which holds across DuckDB versions.

# Test 4: All sitting_duck tagged functions have non-empty description
# ===================================================================

query I
SELECT COUNT(*) = 0
FROM duckdb_functions()
WHERE list_contains(categories, 'sitting_duck')
  AND (description IS NULL OR description = '');
----
true
